17:31.368 --> 17:32.769
He doesn't like you.

17:33.103 --> 17:34.171
Sorry.

17:34.171 --> 17:36.407
I don't like you either.

17:36.407 --> 17:38.275
You don't even know me.

17:38.275 --> 17:39.776
You know what?
That's fair.

17:40.277 --> 17:42.779
I'm Pig Nose,
and this is my
brother-in-law, Scott.

17:42.779 --> 17:44.281
He's visiting
from Hoth.

17:44.281 --> 17:45.782
I don't know why
they call it Hoth.

17:45.782 --> 17:47.284
They should
call it Coldth.

17:47.785 --> 17:48.786
Okay, settle down.

17:48.786 --> 17:50.153
I'm up after the band.

17:50.655 --> 17:52.155
Thank you.
We're the Cantina Band.

17:52.155 --> 17:53.657
If you have any requests,
shout 'em out.

17:54.157 --> 17:55.659
(THROWING VOICE)
Play that same song.

17:55.659 --> 17:57.661
All right,
same song, here we go.

17:57.661 --> 18:00.330
(STAR WARSCANTINA MUSIC
PLAYING)

18:02.631 --> 18:05.635
Oh, no, Stormtroopers.
Quick, R2, in here.

18:09.473 --> 18:11.975
This door's locked,
move on to the next one.

18:11.975 --> 18:13.476
Well, maybe they're
behind this door.

18:13.977 --> 18:15.480
I just said it's locked.

18:15.480 --> 18:17.981
Well, can't you
knock or something?

18:17.981 --> 18:18.981
Hello?

18:20.484 --> 18:21.984
Well, I guess
whoever's in there

18:22.486 --> 18:23.988
won't be getting
this giant check

18:23.988 --> 18:25.989
.
from Publisher
s Clearing House

18:25.989 --> 18:28.992
CLEVELAND:
Publishers Clearing House!
QUAGMIRE: Shut up.

18:28.992 --> 18:31.495
Did you hear something
?
I heard voices,
but they've stopped,

18:31.495 --> 18:34.966
so I'm gonna assume
there's no one in there.

18:34.966 --> 18:37.467
Hi, my sexy friend
and I are looking for

18:37.467 --> 18:39.469
a ship to take
us to Alderaan,

18:39.469 --> 18:41.972
and I'm willing
to pay big money.

18:41.972 --> 18:44.006
.
Well, you've come
to the right place

18:44.006 --> 18:46.510
I'm Han Solo,
captain of
the Millennium Falcon

18:46.510 --> 18:48.011
and the only
actor whose career

18:48.512 --> 18:49.778
isn't destroyed
by this movie.

18:49.778 --> 18:51.781
Is it a fast ship?
Are you kidding?

18:52.281 --> 18:54.950
It's the ship that
made the Kessel Run
in less than 12 parsecs.

18:54.950 --> 18:58.822
Um, isn't a parsec a unit
of distance, not time?

18:58.822 --> 19:00.323
(STUTTERING)

19:00.323 --> 19:02.491
Chewie, take these
guys to the ship
and get her ready.

19:02.491 --> 19:04.927
(GARGLING)

19:06.029 --> 19:07.663
Always gargle
before a takeoff.

19:07.663 --> 19:09.365
Wokka, wokka!
All right, let's go.

19:12.536 --> 19:14.537
(IN ALIEN LANGUAGE
)

19:14.537 --> 19:16.873
Greedo, as a matter
of fact, I was just

19:16.873 --> 19:18.541
going to see
Jabba and tell him...

19:18.541 --> 19:21.544
(IN ALIEN LANGUAGE)

19:44.501 --> 19:45.667
Well, what do you think?

19:45.667 --> 19:47.571
What a piece of junk!

19:47.571 --> 19:49.572
Thank you,
this was my brother's.
He died of leukemia.

19:49.572 --> 19:51.072
How do you feel now?

19:51.072 --> 19:53.076
You got any
strawberry milk
in there?

19:53.576 --> 19:55.579
No, but she'll make
0.5 past light speed.

19:55.579 --> 19:57.079
If you want,
I'll show you around,

19:57.079 --> 19:59.015
since no one's
trying to stop
the ship or blast us.

19:59.380 --> 20:01.518
Stop that ship,
blast them.

20:01.518 --> 20:02.518
Oh, now I can't
show you around.

20:03.018 --> 20:04.020
.
Quick, get in the ship

20:20.336 --> 20:22.838
Looks like we got
Imperial Cruisers
on our tail.

20:22.838 --> 20:23.839
Oh, look at that one
on the left.

20:24.339 --> 20:26.842
Get off your cell phone,
you are driving.

20:34.349 --> 20:35.350
(RADAR BEEPING)

20:35.850 --> 20:37.353
They're gaining on us.

20:37.353 --> 20:39.355
We'll be safe enough,
once we make the jump
to hyperspace.

20:39.854 --> 20:41.824
Besides,
I know a few maneuvers
. We'll lose 'em.

20:47.796 --> 20:49.797
That... That was
your maneuver?

20:49.797 --> 20:51.800
Moving slightly
to the left?

20:51.800 --> 20:54.802
?
Well, I mean, we'r
e not in the same
place we were, huh

20:54.802 --> 20:55.804
That ought to
confuse 'em.

20:55.804 --> 20:58.307
Yeah, but you
hardly did anything.

20:58.307 --> 21:01.310
You just started
listing lazily
to the left.

21:01.310 --> 21:03.045
I'm pretty sure
they can keep up.

21:03.045 --> 21:04.545
!
Where did they go?
There they are

21:04.545 --> 21:07.048
They're listing
lazily to the left
. Go left, left!

21:07.048 --> 21:08.983
Boy, this guy
knows some maneuvers.

21:08.983 --> 21:10.151
All right,
strap yourselves in,

21:10.151 --> 21:11.653
I'm about to make
the jump to light speed.

21:11.653 --> 21:14.089
Did he say "strap
in" or "strap on"?

21:21.229 --> 21:23.831
.
Man, hyperspace
always looks so freaky

21:23.931 --> 21:28.269
(DOCTOR WHO THEME PLAYING)

21:38.246 --> 21:42.149
(HIP-HOP BASS BLARING)

21:45.185 --> 21:46.688
Governor Tarkin.

21:46.688 --> 21:49.691
I recognized your
foul stench as soon as
I was brought onboard.

21:49.691 --> 21:53.694
Um, actually, that's me,
I made a Darth doody.

21:53.694 --> 21:55.697
I sithed my pants.

21:55.697 --> 21:58.700
My diaper's gone
over to the dark side.

21:58.700 --> 22:00.468
I got pages of these,
I could go on.

22:00.468 --> 22:02.470
Princess Leia,
we've chosen to test

22:02.470 --> 22:05.473
our Death Star
planet blower-upper gun

22:05.473 --> 22:07.741
on your home
planet of Alderaan.

22:07.909 --> 22:08.910
No!

22:09.176 --> 22:11.279
She said no.
Should we still do it?

22:12.280 --> 22:13.280
Yeah.

22:15.982 --> 22:18.252
(WEAPON CHARGING)

22:26.027 --> 22:28.796
(GASPING)

22:28.796 --> 22:31.799
So, anyway, I says,
"Forget the dental plan,
forget sick leave.

22:31.799 --> 22:35.302
"I just want
a railing. You know,
one railing right here."

22:35.302 --> 22:38.305
Yeah, I know,
I've almost fallen over
that thing so many times.

22:38.305 --> 22:39.806
So, what did they say?

22:39.806 --> 22:42.309
Get this,
they said they're worried
we'd be leaning all day.

22:42.309 --> 22:43.810
They said that?

22:43.810 --> 22:45.312
(SCOFFS)
Yeah.

22:45.312 --> 22:47.280
Well,
none of this will matter
when we're famous singers.

22:51.017 --> 22:52.519
Good evening,
Death Star.

22:53.019 --> 22:56.022
Tonight a special report
on the controversial
attack on Alderaan.

22:56.022 --> 22:58.023
While some
view the attack
as unwarranted,

22:58.023 --> 22:59.527
the Empire has
obtained proof

22:59.527 --> 23:01.027
that Alderaan
was in possession

23:01.027 --> 23:03.029
of weapons of
mass destruction.

23:03.029 --> 23:04.531
And now, let's go to
our five day forecast.

23:05.032 --> 23:05.932
What's the weather like,
Ollie?

23:05.932 --> 23:07.300
Space weather.
Thanks, Ollie.

23:07.300 --> 23:09.302
Coming up,
we'll give you
the road closures

23:09.302 --> 23:11.304
for this week's
Ewok Pride Parade.

23:11.304 --> 23:12.205
Stay with us.

23:18.245 --> 23:19.247
How am I doing?

23:19.247 --> 23:20.747
Just keep your
knees bent.

23:20.747 --> 23:24.752
Imagine you're
spreading butter on
a big piece of bread.

23:24.752 --> 23:25.751
That's it.

23:25.751 --> 23:28.722
Spread that butter
, with the Force.

23:28.722 --> 23:32.325
Ha! You guys seem like
crazy morons to me.

23:32.325 --> 23:34.561
You don't believe
in the Force, do you?

23:34.561 --> 23:36.062
Oh, you mean that thing
you just found out about,

23:36.062 --> 23:37.464
like,
three hours ago, and are now

23:37.964 --> 23:39.265
judging me for
not believing in it?

23:39.265 --> 23:40.867
Do you believe in anything?

23:40.867 --> 23:43.203
Uh, yeah. Didn't you see m
y Cabala bracelet?

23:43.203 --> 23:44.371
What's Cabala?

23:44.371 --> 23:46.373
About $1.75.

23:46.373 --> 23:47.873
Honestly, I have no idea.

23:47.873 --> 23:49.242
.
I'm just a slave to trends

23:52.344 --> 23:53.780
What the hell?

23:53.780 --> 23:57.250
Oh, my God!
We came out of hyperspace
into an asteroid field.

23:57.250 --> 24:02.522
(ELECTRONIC EXPLOSIONS)

24:02.522 --> 24:05.025
Alderaan's been
destroyed by the Empire.

24:05.025 --> 24:07.026
Maybe we should head
for that small moon,

24:07.026 --> 24:09.929
that's clearly
a small moon, and
not anything else.

24:12.998 --> 24:16.336
That's no moon.
It's a space station.

24:19.238 --> 24:21.574
Oh, crap.
They've got us
in a tractor beam.

24:21.574 --> 24:24.243
Well, they're not
going to get me
without a fight.

24:26.079 --> 24:29.682
You can't win.
But there are
alternatives to fighting.

24:30.016 --> 24:30.783
Like what?

24:30.783 --> 24:33.352
Like getting
the hell out of here!

24:34.854 --> 24:36.355
No, just kidding.

24:36.355 --> 24:37.790
?
Can you imagine
if I was like that

25:14.994 --> 25:15.996
(LASERS FIRING)

25:15.996 --> 25:18.697
(BODIES THUDDING)

25:18.697 --> 25:21.200
PETER: All right,
just follow my lea
d and act real cool.

25:21.700 --> 25:25.203
(MINNIE THE MOOCHER PLAYING)

25:43.889 --> 25:46.391
All right,
I'm gonna go knock out
that tractor beam.

25:46.391 --> 25:48.327
And we'll go
rescue the princess.

25:48.327 --> 25:52.331
You know, Luke, this
may be the last time
we see each other.

25:52.331 --> 25:54.832
So there's something
I want you to know.

25:54.832 --> 26:00.706
?? Now I've had
the time of my life

26:00.706 --> 26:05.810
?? And I owe it all to you

26:07.812 --> 26:09.981
?? I've been waiting
for so long

26:09.981 --> 26:12.217
?? Now I've
finally found someone

26:12.217 --> 26:14.052
?? To stand by me

26:16.588 --> 26:18.656
?? So we take
each other's hand

26:19.157 --> 26:24.362
?? 'Cause we seem to understand
the urgency

26:24.562 --> 26:26.930
?? Just remember

26:26.930 --> 26:30.535
?? You're the one thing

26:30.535 --> 26:35.473
?? I can't get enough of

26:35.473 --> 26:40.477
?? So I'll tell you something

26:40.477 --> 26:44.782
?? This could be love because

26:44.782 --> 26:49.821
?? I've had
the time of my life

26:49.821 --> 26:53.758
?? No,
I never felt this way before

26:53.758 --> 26:58.596
?? Yes, I swear
it's the truth

26:58.596 --> 27:04.302
?
?? And I owe it all to you ?

27:06.971 --> 27:07.472
(SQUEAKING)

27:10.073 --> 27:11.375
(GROWLS)

27:11.375 --> 27:13.378
Holy shit!

27:16.813 --> 27:18.816
You ain't never
gonna believe
what I just seen.

27:18.816 --> 27:20.318
Tyra Banks?

27:20.318 --> 27:21.819
See, now you say
something better,

27:21.819 --> 27:23.321
so my thing don't
sound cool no more.

27:23.321 --> 27:24.821
Oh! Come on,
what did you see?

27:24.821 --> 27:25.823
I don't remember.

27:26.323 --> 27:28.326
I just was thinking
about Tyra Banks.

27:28.326 --> 27:29.326
(EXCLAIMS)

27:29.827 --> 27:30.827
Can you imagine?

27:30.827 --> 27:32.329
Every night!

27:32.329 --> 27:33.330
Don't shake my hand.

27:33.330 --> 27:35.333
You ain't got no hand!
You a little truck.

27:38.902 --> 27:40.337
BRIAN: So, what are we on,
the first floor?

27:40.337 --> 27:42.306
CHRIS: We are
on the second floor.

27:42.306 --> 27:45.909
PETER: No, no, no,
here's the Banana Republic,
and we just passed that.

27:45.909 --> 27:49.280
It's right back there.
We parked on the Macy's side,

27:49.280 --> 27:51.548
so now we must be over here
by the JCPenney.

27:51.983 --> 27:54.451
CHRIS: It looks like
the first floor is
mostly men's stuff,

27:54.451 --> 27:56.253
and there's
a Lady Foot Locker
right over there.

27:56.253 --> 27:57.789
BRIAN: All right,
so we're on the third floor.

27:58.156 --> 27:59.690
All right,
let's get in
the elevator.

27:59.690 --> 28:02.526
And hurry up, 'cause
the smell of that Mrs.
Fields is killing me.

28:02.959 --> 28:06.464
(THE IMPERIAL MARCH
MUZAK PLAYING)

28:24.314 --> 28:26.049
Wrong floor.
Stormtrooper church.

28:26.049 --> 28:28.051
And do you,
Allen, take Judith

28:28.051 --> 28:30.053
to be your
lawfully wedded wife

28:30.053 --> 28:33.156
till death or a giant
explosion do you part?

28:40.029 --> 28:42.466
Where are you
taking this thing?

28:42.466 --> 28:45.001
Prisoner transfer
from cell block 1138.

28:45.001 --> 28:46.937
You think you could get me
a room by the pool?

28:46.937 --> 28:47.938
(LAUGHING)

28:48.437 --> 28:50.640
Is funny,
because you are a prisoner

28:51.141 --> 28:53.376
and there is no pool
because is Death Star.

28:54.110 --> 28:55.911
(MOANS)

28:55.911 --> 28:58.414
We've gotta find out
what cell this princes
s of yours is in.

28:58.414 --> 28:59.915
There it is, 2187.

28:59.915 --> 29:00.917
I'm on it!

29:00.917 --> 29:02.418
Everything's
under control here.

29:02.918 --> 29:04.421
Situation normal.

29:04.421 --> 29:05.421
STORM TROOPER:
What happened?

29:05.421 --> 29:07.424
We had a slight
weapons malfunction,

29:07.424 --> 29:09.925
but everything's
perfectly all right.
We're fine.

29:09.925 --> 29:13.430
We're all fine here now.
Thank you.

29:13.430 --> 29:14.930
How are you?

29:14.930 --> 29:17.167
(GROANING)
I've been better.

29:17.300 --> 29:18.300
Well, tell me what's up.

29:18.300 --> 29:19.970
Well,
I'm in this relationship

29:19.970 --> 29:21.971
and it doesn't seem
to be going anywhere.

29:22.471 --> 29:24.974
I like her, but we're
not really connecting.

29:24.974 --> 29:26.977
How long has it been?
About 10 months.

29:26.977 --> 29:28.477
And how often do
you see each other?

29:28.477 --> 29:29.980
Couple times a week.

29:29.980 --> 29:31.480
Well, why don't you try
seeing each other
a little more often,

29:31.981 --> 29:33.482
and see if you
connect a little more?

29:33.482 --> 29:35.385
And if not,
it may be time to move on.

29:35.385 --> 29:36.619
Thanks for calling.

29:37.119 --> 29:38.821
This is Han Solo
and I'm gonna be
keeping you company

29:38.821 --> 29:42.057
for the next few hours
, right here on
the midnight shift.

29:42.057 --> 29:47.562
?? Something's telling m
e it might be you

29:47.562 --> 29:51.734
?? It's telling me
it might be you ??

29:53.769 --> 29:55.770
Aren't you a little fa
t to be a Stormtrooper?

29:56.272 --> 29:58.273
Well, stay here and rot,
you stuck-up bitch.

29:58.273 --> 29:59.775
Wait, who are you?

29:59.775 --> 30:01.276
I'm Luke Skywalker.

30:01.276 --> 30:03.778
Me and Han Solo
and Obi-Wan are
here to rescue you.

30:03.778 --> 30:05.281
Wait, Obi-Wan Kenobi?

30:05.281 --> 30:06.282
Yeah!

30:06.781 --> 30:08.685
Suddenly,
I'm not so fat, huh?

30:18.727 --> 30:20.728
Come on,
into the garbage chute.

30:23.598 --> 30:25.067
She's right!
Come on, Chewbacca.

30:25.067 --> 30:26.067
What, are you kidding?
It's probably

30:26.067 --> 30:27.536
full of disease.
I'm not jumping in there.

30:27.969 --> 30:29.972
Not even if I
throw this pig's ear?

30:29.972 --> 30:31.472
Oh, come on,
that's not fair.
Go get it!

30:31.973 --> 30:33.408
(BARKING)

30:35.711 --> 30:37.212
Oh, boy!
Great idea, Princess,

30:37.212 --> 30:38.713
diving into
a pile of garbage.

30:38.713 --> 30:40.716
Hey, when we get out of here,
maybe you can show me around

30:40.716 --> 30:41.716
your home planet of Alderaan.

30:42.218 --> 30:43.218
Aww...

30:43.218 --> 30:44.219
Too soon?

30:44.720 --> 30:45.720
Hey, it could be worse.

30:45.720 --> 30:47.723
(MECHANICAL ECHOING)

30:47.723 --> 30:49.024
It's worse.

30:52.360 --> 30:54.362
The walls are closing.

30:54.362 --> 30:55.363
(ALL SCREAMING)

30:56.965 --> 30:58.233
LOIS: Oh, my God!

30:58.233 --> 30:59.235
Listen to them,
R2, they're dying!

30:59.734 --> 31:00.735
What do we do?

31:00.735 --> 31:02.737
Only one thing
to do, man.

31:02.737 --> 31:04.740
You still got
that bag I gave you?

31:09.444 --> 31:10.945
Man, I wish I could
listen to some

31:11.446 --> 31:13.948
Tatooine,
Wind & Fire right now.

31:13.948 --> 31:15.451
Hmm.

31:15.451 --> 31:17.952
So, you think
the Empire's gonna
fall, man?

31:17.952 --> 31:20.956
(STUTTERING)
I don't know, man.

31:20.956 --> 31:23.458
How you doing
right now?

31:23.458 --> 31:25.460
Good. Why?

31:25.460 --> 31:28.963
I think I may be
having sort of a
mini freak-out here.

31:29.465 --> 31:30.464
Oh.

31:30.464 --> 31:33.468
Just tell me I
don't have to stay
in this room.

31:33.468 --> 31:34.970
What?
Just tell me,
right now,

31:34.970 --> 31:36.471
that I don't have
to stay in this room.

31:36.971 --> 31:38.472
You don't have to
stay in this room.

31:38.972 --> 31:40.442
Oh, thank Christ!

31:43.845 --> 31:44.846
(ALL CHEERING)

31:46.547 --> 31:48.650
.
Thank God! We're saved

31:49.150 --> 31:51.986
Look at this.
Who throws out half a pizza?

31:51.986 --> 31:53.488
.
And look at this couch

31:53.488 --> 31:56.491
Somebody threw out
a whole couch and
it's in great shape.

31:56.491 --> 31:58.993
Yeah, you put
a little Febreze on that,
scrub it out a little bit,

31:58.993 --> 32:00.495
it would look grea
t in your apartment.

32:00.495 --> 32:03.497
You know what? I know
we have a dangerous
job to do here,

32:03.997 --> 32:07.702
but I'm taking this.
I'm taking this couch.

32:07.702 --> 32:11.172
PETER: All right, ready?
All right, one, two, three.

32:11.172 --> 32:13.674
Okay! Easy, easy, easy...

32:13.674 --> 32:15.008
Easy, easy...
Wait! Wait, wait...

32:15.008 --> 32:16.044
Stop! Stop, stop...

32:16.044 --> 32:17.045
What? What, what?

32:17.544 --> 32:19.046
No, no, no.
Twist it.
I am.

32:19.046 --> 32:21.049
No, no, no.
The other way.

32:21.049 --> 32:22.450
Which way?
You're twisting
the wrong way.

32:22.450 --> 32:23.952
What do you
want me to do?

32:23.952 --> 32:25.953
Just look down, look at me,
look what I'm doing.

32:25.953 --> 32:27.454
All right,
see the way I'm twisting it?
Yeah.

32:27.454 --> 32:29.624
Right, turn it that
way from your end.
Okay.

32:29.624 --> 32:33.728
No, no, no. Just put
it down,

32:33.728 --> 32:34.728
just drop it.
Yeah, yeah, okay.

32:34.728 --> 32:35.629
All right, all right.

32:35.629 --> 32:37.431
All right, let's...

32:37.431 --> 32:38.832
Just hang on and
figure this out.

32:38.832 --> 32:41.335
Han, there are
Stormtroopers
all over the place.

32:41.335 --> 32:42.836
Shouldn't we be
getting out of here?

32:42.836 --> 32:46.340
.
All right, okay,
all right,
I got it, I know..

32:46.340 --> 32:47.342
.
Here's what we're gonna do

32:47.342 --> 32:48.809
We're going to
take the cushions off,

32:49.242 --> 32:51.178
unscrew the legs,
take the mattress out,

32:51.578 --> 32:53.580
and this whole thing
is going to be
a lot simpler.

32:53.580 --> 32:55.048
It's easier than
we're making it.

33:12.132 --> 33:14.901
(POWER DRAINING)

33:16.703 --> 33:18.206
Hey, did you
hear something?

33:18.206 --> 33:20.707
Probably just
another drill.

33:20.707 --> 33:22.709
You know that
last drill we had?

33:22.709 --> 33:25.712
I was about to
finally bone
my girlfriend,

33:25.712 --> 33:28.215
and then we heard
that there was
this drill

33:28.715 --> 33:31.385
and she told me
there was no way.

33:37.324 --> 33:40.660
STEWIE: So, Obi-Wan,
we meet again.

33:40.660 --> 33:42.662
What part of,
"Stay 50 yards away

33:42.662 --> 33:44.965
"at all times,"
don't you understand?

33:46.966 --> 33:48.401
Uh-oh!

33:48.401 --> 33:50.804
Your powers are weak,
old man.

33:53.973 --> 33:55.241
!
CHRIS: Obi-Wan

33:56.742 --> 33:59.578
Boy,
you got here just in time.

34:00.546 --> 34:02.281
No!

34:11.258 --> 34:13.592
Right! Go! Go, go, go.

34:16.630 --> 34:17.831
All right, twist it
counter-clockwise.

34:17.831 --> 34:19.499
I am twisting it,
you're twisting
it the other way.

34:19.499 --> 34:22.868
I mean counter-clockwise
from where I'm standing...
So then you...

34:23.302 --> 34:24.805
So clockwise.
So, yeah! Okay,
all right.

34:24.805 --> 34:26.672
Yeah, so
you twist it clockwise.

34:26.672 --> 34:29.508
Okay. Go!
You know what?
Put it down.

34:29.508 --> 34:31.510
Put it down for a sec.
My fingers
are killing me.

34:31.510 --> 34:32.912
.
Han, they're
shooting at us

34:32.912 --> 34:34.313
All right, you know what?
Lift it up tall-ways.

34:36.749 --> 34:39.019
For Christ's...
It's wedged. It's wedged.

34:39.019 --> 34:41.020
All right, okay.
You know what?
It's not going anywhere.

34:41.020 --> 34:42.587
Let's just take off,
we'll deal with it later.

34:42.587 --> 34:44.658
You get in the cockpit,
and I'll just...

34:44.658 --> 34:46.492
I'll hang onto
this thing as we go.

34:58.271 --> 34:59.270
Easy!

35:10.148 --> 35:12.151
I can't believe he's gone.

35:12.151 --> 35:15.653
I know, Luke,
but it's true, he's gone.

35:16.154 --> 35:17.656
I mean,
you saw him get beheaded.

35:17.656 --> 35:19.658
Nobody lives
through that.

35:19.658 --> 35:21.160
Not for long anyway.

35:21.659 --> 35:23.662
I mean, sometimes
the brain is still active

35:23.662 --> 35:26.165
for a few minutes
after the beheading,

35:26.165 --> 35:29.168
but to be honest,
I can't imagine
a worse kind of hell.

35:29.168 --> 35:32.670
And unfortunately,
hell is probably
where he'll end up,

35:32.670 --> 35:34.172
because
the Christians don't look

35:34.172 --> 35:36.609
too kindly on
the whole Force thing.

35:36.609 --> 35:38.911
Come on, kid,
we're not out
of the woods yet.

35:42.747 --> 35:43.748
Here they come.

35:44.250 --> 35:49.154
(HUMMING STAR WARS
BATTLE THEME)

36:00.765 --> 36:02.100
Hey, Han!
What?

36:02.100 --> 36:03.601
Why do they call
them TIE fighters?

36:04.035 --> 36:05.003
No idea.

36:05.003 --> 36:09.741
(SPEAKING THAI)

36:17.382 --> 36:19.285
They're coming too fast!

36:19.285 --> 36:21.119
A nickel for every time
I've had that problem.

36:21.119 --> 36:22.054
Just keep shooting, Luke.

36:29.761 --> 36:33.199
Yeah! That's how we do it
in my neighborhood, bitch!

36:37.669 --> 36:39.303
I got him! I got him!

36:39.736 --> 36:41.172
Right, kid. Don't get penisy.

36:46.844 --> 36:48.846
I just want to tell
you both, good luck!

36:48.846 --> 36:50.714
We're all counting on you.

37:11.768 --> 37:12.769
(EXHALES)

37:16.941 --> 37:19.444
Mom? Yeah, we won.

37:19.943 --> 37:21.946
Yeah, we won the battle.

37:21.946 --> 37:23.947
Yeah,
I'm calling, like you asked.

37:23.947 --> 37:25.950
Okay. Okay.

37:25.950 --> 37:27.452
Okay, but I gotta go.

37:27.452 --> 37:29.453
I got other stuff to do.

37:29.453 --> 37:33.457
.
Okay.
Okay, but I gotta go. Okay

37:33.457 --> 37:36.460
Okay. Yes. Yes.

37:36.960 --> 37:38.962
Yes. Yes,
Mom. I love you, too, Mom.

37:39.463 --> 37:41.232
Okay. All right. Goodbye.

37:41.366 --> 37:42.332
(EXHALES)

37:45.937 --> 37:48.939
The Homing Beacon
is safely on board
theMillennium Falcon.

37:49.439 --> 37:51.442
I'm taking
an awful risk, Vader.

37:51.442 --> 37:53.443
It'd better work.

37:53.443 --> 37:54.945
You know,
I think they
took your old couch.

37:54.945 --> 37:56.446
What? I threw that away.

37:56.948 --> 37:59.450
Yeah, it was weird.
I just killed Obi-Wan,
and then I look over

37:59.450 --> 38:01.952
and there are these
two dudes scurrying
across with a couch.

38:01.952 --> 38:04.956
It had a stain on it,
from when we had
Hawaiian Punch night.

38:04.956 --> 38:07.859
Yeah, that's my couch.
Rebel scum.

38:29.379 --> 38:30.880
)
(IMITATES LASER FIRING

38:30.880 --> 38:32.249
Gotcha!

38:34.951 --> 38:38.455
Thanks to the information
in this R2 unit provided
by Princess Leia,

38:38.955 --> 38:41.957
we should be able to mount
a successful offensive
on the Death Star.

38:42.458 --> 38:46.263
But first, please take
a moment to watch
this instructional video.

38:51.335 --> 38:53.336
Nothing but net.

38:53.336 --> 38:58.342
Hi! I'm Magic Johnson
with a few tips on
blowing up the Death Star.

38:58.342 --> 39:01.844
First off,
never forget your objective.

39:01.844 --> 39:03.346
There are gonna
be so many folks

39:03.346 --> 39:05.349
coming at you
to slow you down,

39:05.848 --> 39:09.353
you might feel like you go
t a bull's-eye on your head.

39:09.353 --> 39:12.855
No, but they will be
trying to kill you.

39:12.855 --> 39:16.859
Also, don't forget
you have teammates
out there watching your back.

39:16.859 --> 39:18.361
Unless you've
been messing around

39:18.361 --> 39:20.863
with their wife
or girlfriend.

39:20.863 --> 39:23.866
No, but they will
be there to help you.

39:24.368 --> 39:26.869
Lastly, you wanna make sur
e you step back

39:26.869 --> 39:29.372
and take cover after
you sink that bucket.

39:29.372 --> 39:33.376
'Cause that sky
gonna light up
like the Fourth of July.

39:33.376 --> 39:37.447
No, but there will
be a large explosion.

39:37.447 --> 39:38.447
Any questions?

39:38.447 --> 39:39.916
.
Yeah, I got a question

39:39.916 --> 39:42.886
Does Barry Manilow kno
w you raid his wardrobe?

39:44.553 --> 39:46.889
You'll get
the answer to that question
next Saturday.

39:46.889 --> 39:48.492
(SCOFFS)

39:48.492 --> 39:50.493
Don't mess with the bull,
young man,
you'll get the horns.

40:00.703 --> 40:02.038
Biggs? Jesus!

40:02.038 --> 40:03.539
What the hell
happened to you?

40:03.539 --> 40:07.042
Oh! Hey, Luke. I was
under a Y-wing working
on the space engine,

40:07.042 --> 40:09.044
.
and the whole thin
g just dropped on me

40:09.044 --> 40:10.546
Holy crap!

40:10.546 --> 40:12.047
Yeah. Holy crap.

40:12.548 --> 40:15.050
?
So, you here for
the Death Star assault

40:15.050 --> 40:16.551
Yeah, yeah,
I can't wait.

40:16.551 --> 40:17.553
How about you?

40:18.053 --> 40:20.055
Well, no,
I can't really...

40:20.055 --> 40:21.557
Oh, yeah,
because of that...

40:21.557 --> 40:22.557
The chair.
Chair, yeah.

40:23.058 --> 40:24.560
Yeah, so
I'll just be here
making sandwiches

40:24.560 --> 40:26.061
for when you guys
get back.

40:26.061 --> 40:27.563
Oh...

40:27.563 --> 40:29.064
Well, that's cool.

40:29.064 --> 40:30.065
Yeah.

40:30.065 --> 40:31.567
You want anything special?

40:31.567 --> 40:33.568
What?
You mean like a sandwich?

40:33.568 --> 40:36.070
Yeah.
Oh, no, I mean,
I couldn't...

40:36.070 --> 40:38.873
You know, whatever
you make will be fine.

40:39.174 --> 40:40.675
Hey, Biggs.
Yeah?

40:40.675 --> 40:43.678
You're just as big
a part of this as...

40:43.678 --> 40:47.182
I mean, you're doing stuff,
and I think that's great!

40:50.251 --> 40:52.221
Well, kid,
I guess this is goodbye.

40:52.221 --> 40:54.689
So, you got your rewar
d and you're leaving?
Is that it?

40:55.090 --> 40:56.090
When you say it
that way, I sound like

40:56.591 --> 40:58.093
a douche, but, yeah,
that's what I'm doing.

40:58.093 --> 41:00.094
What did you get
for a reward, anyway?

41:00.094 --> 41:04.499
Let's see.
I got 10% off
a Netflix membership,

41:04.999 --> 41:07.168
some nice
Cracker Barrel Cheddar,

41:07.168 --> 41:08.670
assorted lotions,

41:08.670 --> 41:12.174
and a little plastic
champagne bottle
full of jelly beans,

41:12.174 --> 41:16.177
and a little bear.
See? Little bear.

41:16.177 --> 41:18.680
"Hey, Luke, we had
fun on the Death Star."

41:19.180 --> 41:20.682
.
Well,
take care of yourself, Han

41:20.682 --> 41:23.485
I guess that's
what you're best at.

41:23.585 --> 41:25.988
Oh, look!
A light saber cheese knife!

41:29.991 --> 41:30.825
Yuck!

41:45.607 --> 41:46.641
All wings, check in.

41:46.641 --> 41:47.910
Red Three standing by.

41:47.910 --> 41:48.909
Red Six standing by.

41:49.344 --> 41:50.679
Red Five standing by.

41:50.679 --> 41:52.080
Red Buttons standing by.

41:52.080 --> 41:53.415
Redd Foxx standing by.

41:53.415 --> 41:54.681
Big Red standing by.

41:54.681 --> 41:56.050
SEAN CONNERY:
Red Octoberstanding by.

41:56.384 --> 41:57.785
Helen Reddy standing by.

41:57.785 --> 41:59.153
Simply Red standing by.

42:29.817 --> 42:32.252
I'm going in.
Cover me, Porkins.

42:32.252 --> 42:34.588
Having a little trouble here.

42:46.133 --> 42:47.134
Careful, Redd Foxx!

42:47.134 --> 42:49.070
There's one
right on your tail.

42:54.408 --> 42:56.610
I'm coming, Elizabeth!

43:04.216 --> 43:06.719
HERBERT: Use the Force, Luke.

43:06.719 --> 43:07.721
Obi-Wan?

43:07.721 --> 43:11.726
Yeah, it's me. Use the Force.

43:11.726 --> 43:15.227
Force that thing in there,
just like I showed
you with those puppets.

43:15.729 --> 43:18.732
But don't tell nobody 'cause
you'll get in trouble.

43:26.439 --> 43:28.941
Clark,
I don't like the look
of this neighborhood.

43:28.941 --> 43:30.444
Come on, Ellen
, it's important
for the kids

43:30.444 --> 43:32.446
to witness the plight
of the Rebellion.

43:32.446 --> 43:34.880
Kids, you noticing
all this plight?

43:34.880 --> 43:35.816
Roll 'em up!

43:42.322 --> 43:44.690
The Force is
strong with this one.

43:47.594 --> 43:48.394
(YELLING)

43:48.861 --> 43:50.129
Fuck you,
you son of a bitch!

43:50.564 --> 43:52.032
What am I, R2Pac?

43:52.032 --> 43:54.300
COMPUTER: The Death Star
is getting closer.

43:54.300 --> 43:57.169
And Leia's getting larger.

44:08.915 --> 44:10.916
I have you now,
young Skywalker.

44:10.916 --> 44:14.321
And with today's gas prices,
not a minute too soon.

44:16.789 --> 44:17.556
What the deuce?

44:18.725 --> 44:20.026
(WHOOPING)

44:20.292 --> 44:21.294
Look at us.
Look at how much more

44:21.794 --> 44:23.496
.
comfortable we are
now shooting stuff

44:50.155 --> 44:51.692
Whew!

44:51.692 --> 44:55.694
HERBERT: Luke, the Force will
be with you always.

44:55.694 --> 44:58.698
And so will I, always.

44:59.198 --> 45:00.700
Of course when you
get older and get

45:01.199 --> 45:04.102
